<title>USA: ReliaStar raises share repurchase program.</title>
<headline>ReliaStar raises share repurchase program.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>ReliaStar Financial Corp said Thursday its board of directors has approved an increase in the company's share repurchase program to $125 million from $100 million.</p>
<p>ReliaStar said in February that it planned to repurchase up to $100 million of ReliaStar common stock in conjunction with the closing of its acquisition of Security-Connecticut Corp.</p>
<p>ReliaStar Financial is the twelfth-largest publicly held life insurance holding company in the United States.</p>
<p>			((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
